From 31b36ee3fa66843e711e4d8319765c8737ac0476 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:44:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Custody is another program: custody-preview build (V4
 hash, version 5)

The previous candidate dispatched the custody instructions in a binary
that embeds RULESET_HASH_V3 and writes program_version 4. Now:

- Default build (S1): RULESET_HASH_V3, version 4, rules 12; the custody
  tags 0xC1-0xCB are BadData before any account is read, and the custody
  amendments to SettleCaravan, settle_raid and CloseVault are compiled
  out (behaviour of the 4cd901de S1 program; the .so is not compared).
- Feature custody-preview: RULESET_HASH_V4 (2f430c06...fdf48635, pinned
  in frontier-abi against ruleset_hash_v4), program_version 5, rules 13,
  custody dispatched. Its prologue refuses every S1 season and the S1
  program refuses every custody season (RulesetMismatch).
- Marker PSF_CUSTODY_PREVIEW_BUILD: build-frontier.sh refuses it as a
  deployable artefact, as it refuses the test builds.
- Test: the vault stock writers are SendCaravan's debit, SettleCaravan's
  clamped credit and custody's write-back; a new writer fails it (the
  lots' room is reserved only while every writer keeps STORES +
  CUSTODY_QUOTA <= CAP).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
